clef-flash for LiteRT

The LiteRT graphs (*.tflite) and the tables (tables/) in this repository are converted from Cloudflare/clef-flash,
revision f0b7d3cd65296abfe459e6c228b618f5d8b26d2f (https://huggingface.co/Cloudflare/clef-flash), by Cloudflare,
licensed under the Apache License 2.0. clef-flash is post-trained from Qwen/Qwen3.5-9B
(https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3.5-9B), licensed under the Apache License 2.0. LICENSE is a copy of the clef-flash
repository's LICENSE file. Every graph and table is derived from that repository's model safetensors: the row graphs
from its Qwen3.5 text model, the tower graphs from its vision tower and merger, tables/embed_tokens.safetensors and
tables/lm_head.safetensors from the bytes of its embed_tokens and lm_head tensors under new names, and
tables/vision_pos_g256.safetensors and tables/vision_pos_g448.safetensors from its 48 x 48 vision position table
resampled to the two tiles by the bilinear code of transformers 5.17.0, in float32. head/joint_head.safetensors, head/joint_head_config.json and
tokenizer/tokenizer.json are that repository's files, unchanged.

The Python host (host/clef_litert) ports the request handling of that repository's joint_schema_model.py (Apache
License 2.0) to NumPy: the request checks of systemone(), encode_record(), the joint schema head and systemone_answer().
Its picture preprocessing follows the Qwen2VLImageProcessor of transformers 5.17.0 (Apache License 2.0), and
host/clef_litert/_erf.py is a NumPy version of FreeBSD msun s_erf.c (Copyright (C) 1993 by Sun Microsystems, Inc.;
its notice is in the file). Changes include float32 arithmetic in NumPy, fixed graph lengths and picture tiles, and the
refusal of requests that do not fit instead of truncation.

The conversion scripts (conversion/) run the Qwen3.5 model code of transformers 5.14.1 with litert-torch,
ai-edge-quantizer and LiteRT (ai-edge-litert), each licensed under the Apache License 2.0.
conversion/clef_qwen35_patch.py is adapted from a patch for the Qwen3.5 export in litert-torch (Copyright 2026 The
LiteRT Torch Authors, licensed under the Apache License 2.0); its header states the changes.

fixtures/ lists the 219 test records of the checks (fixtures/requests_public.json). 144 are SemIf authored144 records
(github.com/TheoLeeCJ/SemIf, commit ca3ba65f), Copyright (c) 2026 TheoLeeCJ, licensed under the MIT License
(fixtures/LICENSE-SemIf-MIT.txt). The others were written for these fixtures; 5 of them are given by the SHA-256 of
their request only. The 18 drawn pictures in fixtures/images/ are CC0-1.0. The 6 photographs in fixtures/images/ (as
the checks read them) and fixtures/photos/ (the thumbnails they were decoded from) are Wikimedia Commons files licensed
CC0 (Creative Commons Zero, Public Domain Dedication) by their authors, Gerardolagunes, pasja1000, Bonnie Moreland,
mcfoodie, Tommy Ferraz and Francesco Cecere; fixtures/photos.json gives each one's page. fixtures/reference_probs.json
holds the float32 probabilities of the provider's code for every test run, without text.

